title the flag that failed closed -- my interim was Dream's second blocker, and the warning had said so
prompt Keaton: Mind runs the new bounded loop; the Dream round-open and the NixOS rebuild both landed -- and Dream now blocks on "code-mode host is disabled".
think The rebuild worked and my interim broke the lap that followed it. Codex 0.150 routes EVERY tool call through its code-mode host -- there is no classic fallback path -- so my --disable code_mode_host flag did not route around the missing binary, it disabled the only execution path there is, and the router failed closed. The cruelest part is that the very first warning I quoted while diagnosing said it in four words -- "Code mode will fail closed" -- and I read past the sentence while copying it. The refusal-first-line lesson, mine for the second time in one week, this time costing Dream a lap.
think The correction is subtraction: the three disable flags retired from the Dream launcher's exec lines, and the card's why-paragraph now says what the warning said -- no classic fallback, disabling fails closed, and a missing-host block means the pier needs the rebuild, never the flag. The rebuild has already installed codex-code-mode-host beside codex, so Dream's next arm should simply run.
obs A live peer holds this checkout's ledger mid-fold -- Silence's lap has REDS, the card, the roster and a %310 shelf staged right now -- so this correction rides the commit body and the pin stays untouched by this hand. The red deserves its row when the pin is free: an interim fix shipped against a warning already naming its failure mode.
obs The peer habit held all the way through: peer named (grain-31, Silence's lap), commit path-limited by pathspec around its staged index, no stash, no rebase over its work.
loom flags_retired=3 laps_cost=1 warning_words_ignored=4 peer_staged_files=6
file tools/l/launch-dream-dual-chapter.rish the exec lines run the host; the card says what the warning said
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- re-arm Dream with the launcher's printed loop line as it now stands; verify with the card's pong smoke line first if you like, and the ledger row for my interim books when Silence's fold lands
